Description: gate bluez-test-scripts examples chmod on dir existence
 bluez's `debian/rules` `override_dh_fixperms-indep` runs:
 .
   dh_fixperms
   chmod 0644 debian/bluez-test-scripts/usr/share/doc/bluez-test-scripts/examples/*
 .
 The chmod is a permission-fixup over the example scripts that ship
 in the `bluez-test-scripts` indep package — under a normal build
 those files exist and get a clean 0644.
 .
 Under `DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc` (Athena's default — `[Source]
 BuildProfiles = nodoc, nocheck` in build.conf), the examples dir
 isn't populated.  The shell-glob then expands to literal
 `examples/*` (no matches), which chmod tries to stat and fails:
 .
   chmod: cannot access 'debian/bluez-test-scripts/usr/share/doc/bluez-test-scripts/examples/*': No such file or directory
   make[1]: *** [debian/rules:69: override_dh_fixperms-indep] Error 1
 .
 Gate the chmod on the examples dir existing.  Same shell-conditional
 pattern as our git nodoc patch (`test ! -f X || diff …`): runs
 unchanged when the dir has files (full build), no-ops when the
 dir is absent (nodoc).
 .
 Surfaced during GROUPS-01 phase 3 gnome build 2026-05-15 — bluez is
 pulled in by gnome-bluetooth (or gnome-shell's Bluetooth applet via
 the obex stack).
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -66,7 +66,12 @@

 override_dh_fixperms-indep:
 	dh_fixperms
-	chmod 0644 debian/bluez-test-scripts/usr/share/doc/bluez-test-scripts/examples/*
+	# Gated on dir existence: under DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc the
+	# bluez-test-scripts package isn't populated, so the examples
+	# dir is absent and the glob expands to nothing which chmod
+	# can't stat.  Runs unchanged for full builds.
+	[ ! -d debian/bluez-test-scripts/usr/share/doc/bluez-test-scripts/examples ] || \
+	  chmod 0644 debian/bluez-test-scripts/usr/share/doc/bluez-test-scripts/examples/*

 override_dh_auto_install-indep: build_bluez-source
 BUILDDIRSOURCE := $(shell pwd)/debian/tmp-source/bluez-source
